## 12. Measurement

This factory is measured against the **quality criteria** — 13 criteria in 4
families, scored 0–4 — plus **factory-specific measures** it adds for its own
domain. The criteria live outside this factory, in the template project; this
section states only what this factory must *do* about them.

| Requirement | Detail |
|---|---|
| **A scored baseline exists** | Record a score at bootstrap, in the repo, with the date |
| **Re-scoring is a scheduled job** | §7 — daily to start, relaxed once the numbers are stable |
| **Measures are declared, not implied** | Every number this factory tracks is named here or in its ontology, with the decision it informs |
| **A measure with no decision attached is dropped** | Dashboards are not controls; an unused number is maintenance with no payoff |
| **The score is a diff, not an impression** | Recorded in the repo so drift shows up as a change, not a memory |

**Scope note.** This factory measures *its own effectiveness and health* — not
the peculiarities of the work it does. The domain detail is this factory's own
business, handled by its `HQ`; what travels back up is the score and the
template law it implies.

